<title>FINLAND: Kemira says one worker died in blast.</title>
<headline>Kemira says one worker died in blast.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish chemicals group Kemira Oy said in a statement on Tuesday that one worker died in an explosion at a plant in Rotterdam run by its Kemira Pigments B.V. unit.  </p>
<p>Kemira said two workers had also been injured in the explosion.</p>
<p>Earlier on Tuesday afternoon Kemira said three people had been injured in a strong explosion at the Rotterdam plant.</p>
<p>The explosion did not cause any fire. The cause of the blast was unknown, the company said, adding it suspected the accident was connected with maintenance operations.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245</p>
</text>
